<article class="env-lemma" id="0ETF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ETF">Lemma <span data-tag="0ETF">34.10.5</span>.</a> Let $T$ be an affine scheme. Let $\{ T_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$ be a standard V covering. Let $\{ T_{ji} \to T_ j\} _{i = 1, \ldots n_ j}$ be a standard V covering. Then $\{ T_{ji} \to T\} _{i, j}$ is a standard V covering. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows formally from the observation that if $V \subset W$ and $W \subset \Omega $ are extensions of valuation rings, then $V \subset \Omega $ is an extension of valuation rings. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>